<title>USA: Northrop Grumman gets Navy contract.</title>
<headline>Northrop Grumman gets Navy contract.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Northrop Grumman Corp said it got a $23.4 million contract from the U.S. Navy for continued production of its advanced unmanned aerial target, the BQM-74E, and associated air launch kits and technical support data.</p>
<p>The one-year, firm fixed-price contract is for 95 targets. Delivery of the first vehicle under the fiscal year 1997 contract is expected to begin in spring 1998.  This contract is the seventh production order for the BQM-74E target series.</p>
<p>The Navy has bought about 6,600 of Northrop Grumman's BQM-74 family of unmanned aerial vehicles since 1966.</p>
